# Variants — the rule that matters

Every **Save** writes a **new snapshot** with a UTC unix-time id.
Uncommitted work stays on the globe until Save.

**The name is the variant.** Save with the active name and this snapshot
is the next head. Change the name and Save starts another variant. The
list does not nest.

The catalog is append-only: Delete marks a snapshot, `drop` is the only
thing that removes an id. Do not reuse an id. Do not group cards by seed,
parent, or recipe.

The UI word is **Save**, never Update. **variant**, never version.

